  "description": {
    "text": "The English edition of a Japanese set from 1999, sold in 2001 only as a complete collection: a binder holding all 18 cards and six postcards. The cards are cut from six island scenes, three cards to a scene, and each postcard shows one scene whole: Keiko Fukuyama painted the Sky, Riverside and Field of Flowers, and Naoyo Kimura the Jungle, Beach and Sea. One card from each scene is reverse holo.\n\nIn Japan the cards came out in July 1999 for the film Pokémon the Movie 2000 (Revelation Lugia), as two islands: Rainbow Island, Fukuyama's three scenes, and Tropical Island, Kimura's. The English cards keep the Japanese art in a Neo-era frame, and their palm-tree set symbol is drawn in segments where the Japanese one is solid.",
    "sources": [
      {
        "title": "CGC Cards: Registry Featured Set: Southern Islands",
        "url": "https://cgccards.com/news/article/10513/registry-set-august"
      },
      {
        "title": "CGC Cards: Featured Card of the Month: Mew",
        "url": "https://cgccards.com/news/article/11687"
      },
      {
        "title": "The Art of Pokémon: Southern Islands",
        "url": "https://www.artofpkm.com/feature/southern-islands"
      },
      {
        "title": "Serebii: Southern Islands",
